from mk import mk
mk("GoMfKhol88k","Spectral Ambience: Turning Noise into Melodic Synths (Ableton Live 12)",
 "noise-crackle-resonator-instrument-filtered-delayed-noise-into-harmonic-resonator",
 "Effects-only melodic instrument: crackle/noise source → smoothed-random filter → ping-pong feedback delay → spectral harmonic resonator (note, decay, harmonic count, pitch mod) → 'smudge' lo-fi/unison macro → reverb → limiter",
 "Make a playable wind-chime / abstract atmosphere instrument from effects only. Generate vinyl-style crackle (only its density is mapped), or feed any external audio (drums, vocals). Filter it with a resampling-type filter whose cutoff is moved by a sample-and-hold LFO smoothed 100% (random glides), with ~10% drive. Multiply it with a ping-pong delay (6/16, 5/16, down to triplets) at high feedback. Excite a harmonic spectral resonator in note mode, using the granular engine with input quantised, unison 2 and low-damp fixed at 15%. Map fundamental note, decay (blips vs pads), number of harmonics (minimum 6; more = brighter and higher, with high-damp tied to the same macro) and pitch-mod amount (up to 1 semitone) and rate. A 'smudge' macro raises resonator unison spread together with bit/sample-rate reduction (0 = 18 kHz/16-bit, i.e. off). Finish with reverb (size 100, diffusion-network filter on) on time + amount macros, a limiter, macro snapshots and randomisation that excludes note, input level and reverb. Delta vs our click-train comb texture: noise conditioning chain + harmonic resonator macro design.",
 ["Noise/crackle generator or any audio input","Filter with LFO (S&H + smoothing), ping-pong delay with feedback","Harmonic/spectral resonator (Web Audio: bank of high-Q bandpass filters or comb/modal resonators at harmonics of a note, implementation note)","Bit/sample-rate reducer, reverb, limiter, macro rack"],
 [("excitation","audio","Crackle/noise (density control) or external audio such as percussion",True),("note","midi-note","Resonator fundamental (e.g. E0 in the demo)",True)],
 [("resonated_atmos","audio","Bell-like wind chimes, plucks or pad-like resonant atmospheres from noise")],
 ["The resonator only sounds when excited; the level macro controls its input/send amount.","The macro min/max range values were shown only in an on-screen screenshot and are not reproduced. Set ranges by ear; spoken values (6 harmonics minimum, ≤1 st pitch mod, 15% low damp, ~10% drive, 18 kHz/16-bit off point) are kept.","Exclude the note, input level and reverb from randomisation so random snapshots stay usable.","Web Audio resonator mapping is an implementation note, not transcript content."],
 [("Create an effects rack (audio-effect track) with 16 macros. First device: crackle/noise generator; map only its density (crackle level) to a macro. Alternatively route external audio (e.g. bongo drums, vocals) into the rack.","source","Sparse crackle or the external signal"),
  ("Add a filter in a resampling/character mode, LFO wave sample-and-hold with smoothing 100%, drive ~10%. Map cutoff, LFO amount and LFO rate to macros to sculpt which parts of the noise spectrum excite the resonator.","filter","Noise colour drifts smoothly between random positions"),
  ("Add a ping-pong delay at 100% wet. Map delay time (e.g. 6/16, 5/16, limited down to triplets for ambient use), a small L/R delay offset for stereo interest, and feedback (high).","delay","Crackle multiplied into a denser, stereo stream"),
  ("Add the spectral resonator: note mode, granular engine, quantise input on, unison 2, low damp fixed ~15% (cuts boomy lows). Map fundamental note, decay, number of harmonics (min 6) plus high damp on the same macro, pitch-mod amount (up to 1 st) and rate, and input level.","resonator","Pitched bell/chime tones emerge from noise; more harmonics = brighter"),
  ("Add a bit/sample-rate reducer after the resonator. Make one 'smudge' macro that raises the resonator's unison spread, lowers bit depth and lowers sample rate together (0 = 18 kHz/16-bit, i.e. off).","smudge","Wider stereo spread with growing lo-fi grit"),
  ("Add reverb (size 100, diffusion-network filter on) and map decay time and dry/wet, then a final limiter to catch peaks.","space","Long atmospheric tails, protected output"),
  ("Play it: short decay for plucks and blips, long decay for pads. Save macro snapshots of good settings and randomise for new territory, with note, input level and reverb excluded from randomisation.","perform","Range from wind chimes to abstract atmospheres")],
 ["Muting the resonator leaves only filtered/delayed crackle; enabling it produces pitched tones at the set note.","Raising the harmonic count audibly brightens the result.","Smudge at 0 = no bit/sample-rate reduction.","Randomise never changes the fundamental note."],
 ["resonator","spectral","noise","wind-chimes","delay","lofi","macro-rack","web-audio"],
 note="Ableton rack build; macro range table was on-screen only (not in transcript), so only spoken values are recorded.")

mk("U1t3ELd1LDI","The Secret to Endless Ambient Textures in Ableton Live",
 "probability-gated-seeded-scale-loop-endless-ambient-sine-pad",
 "Endless ambient texture from one looping MIDI clip: seeded random notes in a gap-free scale, per-note chance below 50%, randomised velocity/humanise, slow sine pad, scale-degree fifth chording and stereo/granular/reverb chain",
 "Make a single looping MIDI clip never sound the same twice. Generate seeded random notes locked to a scale without half steps (major pentatonic; Dorian also liked), in a mid register (pitch range ~2–3) with long durations. Then lower each note's play chance below 50% (or below 30% for sparse, many-voice clips) and randomise chance, velocity and timing deviation. Play a soft sine pad (~1 s attack, ~6 s release, so sparse notes overlap), add a scale-aware chord effect (scale degree +4 = fifth on every triggered note), then stereo doubling, a parallel echo, a stereo pitch-loop/micro-delay, granular delay (spray up, frequency down) and a big long reverb. For Polyrhythm Studio-style generative scheduling: probability per note, not a fixed sequence.",
 ["Sequencer/clip with per-note probability (Web Audio: scheduler that rolls Math.random() < p per note, implementation note)","Seeded random note generator or a hand-made scale-locked note list","Sine/pad synth with slow attack, long release, enough voices","Chord/interval generator, stereo doubler/chorus, echo, granular delay, long reverb"],
 [("scale","string","Gap-free scale such as major pentatonic or Dorian",True),("clip_length","string","Loop length (bars)",True),("chance","number","Per-note play probability, mostly < 50%",True)],
 [("endless_ambient_loop","audio","Evolving soundscape that varies on every loop pass")],
 ["When you add voices/density after setting chance, chance resets to 100%; re-apply it.","'Fit to scale' re-quantises notes after changing scale.","Sparse clips need long releases so notes still connect.","DAW shortcut and device names are host-specific; the recipe is portable."],
 [("Create a looping MIDI clip and set its scale (e.g. C minor, then switch to major pentatonic or Dorian; scales without half steps suit generative work). Use fit-to-scale after any scale change.","clip","Loop with scale context"),
  ("Generate seeded random notes: set density, pitch register around 2–3 (mid range rather than 0–1), longer durations for smooth pad-like notes, and the number of voices.","generate","Random in-scale notes across the loop"),
  ("Randomise velocities and add deviation/humanise so timing and dynamics wiggle off the grid.","humanise","Expressive, less mechanical notes"),
  ("Select all notes and set chance (play probability) to about 50%, then randomise it so some notes play ~90% and others ~15%. With many voices/density keep chance below 50% or even 30%. Re-apply after regenerating.","chance","Every loop pass plays a different subset"),
  ("Sound: simple sine pad (second oscillator off), attack just over 1 s, release ~6 s, extra voices for overlaps.","synth","Notes float in and out and overlap"),
  ("Add a chord/interval effect before the synth in scale mode with a scale degree of 4 (perfect fifth), so every triggered note becomes a power-fifth.","chord","Denser, stronger polyphony"),
  ("Effects: stereo doubler, parallel echo, a stereo pitch-loop/micro-delay for randomised stereo, granular delay (raise spray, lower frequency) for glitchy texture, then a long-decay reverb.","fx","Wide, evolving ambient soundscape")],
 ["Two consecutive loop passes play audibly different note subsets.","All notes remain in the chosen scale after fit-to-scale.","With chance <30% the texture is sparse but continuous thanks to the 6 s release.","Every triggered note sounds with its fifth when the chord effect is on."],
 ["generative","probability","midi","ambient","pentatonic","sine-pad","polyrhythm-studio","web-audio"],
 note="Patreon/subscribe CTA dropped. Host-specific generator UI mapped to generic per-note probability.")
